# Line-ending policy.
#
# The project checksums its data files with SHA-256 (D-013). Every CSV must
# therefore reach every machine with the same bytes, so Git stores them with
# LF and checks them out with LF on Windows, macOS and Linux. Without this
# file, `core.autocrlf=true` on Windows would write CRLF and the checksums in
# D-013 would only match on one operating system.
*.csv text eol=lf
